.\" SKOMP.1.in  --  man page template for SKOMP
.\" substitute @VERSION@ and @SKOMPHOME@ at build time
.TH SKOMP 1 "@DATE@" "SKOMP @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
skomp \- whole-program R7RS Scheme compiler
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B skomp
[\fB\-t\fR \fITARGDES\fR] [\fB\-c\fR] [\fIOPTION\fR]... \fIFILE\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBskomp\fR compiles one R7RS Scheme program to a native executable or to a
WebAssembly binary.
.PP
\fIFILE\fR is one Scheme program.  The compiler is a whole-program compiler:
it expands the program and every library it imports into a single module, so
there is nothing to compile separately and nothing to link on the Scheme side.
A second input file is an error.
.PP
\fBskomp\fR runs three programs of its own in turn: a Scheme interpreter
hosting the compiler library, the MARV assembler, and \(em for the
WebAssembly target \(em the WCPL linker.  None of the three is on the user's
\fBPATH\fR, and a public copy of any of them installed on the same machine is
neither used nor disturbed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-target =\fITARGDES\fR
Target description name, or a path to a \fI.mvt\fR file.  Default is \fBcl\fR
on Windows and \fBcc\fR elsewhere.
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-target\-dir =\fIDIR\fR
Add \fIDIR\fR to MARV's \fI.mvt\fR lookup path, for target descriptions of
your own.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-compile
Compile to a target object file without linking.  Without \fB\-o\fR the object
is written beside the input with the target's own extension.
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-marv\-source
Stop after writing the MARV module.  Without \fB\-o\fR it is written beside
the input as \fIFILE\fB.mvs\fR.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output =\fIFILE\fR
Output pathname.  Required unless \fB\-c\fR or \fB\-S\fR is given.
.TP
.BI \-O " LEVEL"
Optimization level 0..3 for the backend C compiler, passed to MARV.  It does
not change the Scheme compiler's own code generation.
.TP
.BR \-I ", " \-\-prepend\-libdir =\fIDIR\fR
Prepend \fIDIR\fR to the Scheme library search path.
.TP
.BR \-A ", " \-\-append\-libdir =\fIDIR\fR
Append \fIDIR\fR to the Scheme library search path.
.TP
.BI \-L " DIR"
Synonym for \fB\-A\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-scheme\-optimize= N
The compiler's own optimization level, 0..3.  Default is 1; the other levels
are accepted and validated but not yet interpreted.
.TP
.BI \-\-stack\-pages= N
The size of the compiled program's root stack, in pages.  A page is 65536
words of eight bytes, so the default of 128 pages is 64 MiB.  The minimum is
1.  The stack is a BSS segment, so its pages are touched only as the stack
grows, and a large value costs address space rather than memory or executable
size.  A program that outgrows the stack reports it on standard error and
exits 1; every call that pushes a frame checks the stack against a limit one
red zone short of the end, so nothing is written past the segment first.
.TP
.BI \-\-split\-funcs= N
Passed to MARV: on a \fBcc\fR target, cut the generated C into pieces of at
most \fIN\fR function definitions, each compiled as its own translation unit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print each command before running it.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print the backend commands instead of running them.
.TP
.BR \-M ", " \-\-makefile\-dir =\fIDIR\fR
Write a self-contained build directory with a makefile in \fIDIR\fR instead of
running the backend compiler.  \fIDIR\fR must be empty or not yet exist.
Cannot be combined with \fB\-c\fR or \fB\-S\fR, and requires \fB\-o\fR.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print skomp's version, the commit of each imported part, and the private root
in use.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SKOMP_HOME
The directory holding \fBbin/\fR, \fBlib/\fR and \fBtarget/\fR.  Overrides
both the path compiled in at build time (@SKOMPHOME@) and \fBskomp\-home\fR
beside the executable.
.PP
\fBskomp\fR sets \fBSKINT_LIBDIRS\fR, \fBPATH\fR, \fBWCPL_INCLUDE_PATH\fR and
\fBWCPL_LIBRARY_PATH\fR for the programs it runs, and for those only.
\fBSKINT_LIBDIRS\fR is replaced rather than extended, so a value inherited
from the shell cannot add a library the compiler would then serve.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success.  On failure, the exit code of whichever part failed, or 1 when
that cannot be represented.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I @SKOMPHOME@/bin
The hosted Scheme interpreter, the MARV assembler and the WCPL linker.
.TP
.I @SKOMPHOME@/lib
The compiler library, its own standard library tree, and the Scheme runtime.
.TP
.I @SKOMPHOME@/target
MARV target descriptions.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
skomp \-o app app.scm                 # a native executable
skomp \-t wcpl \-o app.wasm app.scm    # a WASI WebAssembly binary
skomp \-c app.scm                     # a target object file, no link
skomp \-S app.scm                     # stop at the MARV module
skomp \-M build \-o app app.scm        # a self\-contained build directory
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR skint (1)
.PP
The command-line reference, the pipeline and the limits of the compiled
library set are documented in the distribution's \fIdoc/\fR directory and in
\fIlib/skint/compile/README.md\fR.
.SH BUGS
Report at <https://github.com/false-schemers/skomp/issues>.
